{
  "name": "reco-baseline-synthetic",
  "version": 1,
  "description": "Fixed synthetic scenarios for the deterministic recommendation baseline (Phase 10). Signals are hand-built final values (post-window, post-bot-filter), so the pure scorer can be evaluated offline and byte-reproducibly. Golden orderings encode the scorer's full contract: pins dominate, popularity is capped, capture bursts group, ties fall back to recency then photo id. holdout_picks simulate the photos an admin actually selected for a gallery; precision@k against them is the offline relevance check. No real customer data is used anywhere in this dataset.",
  "cases": [
    {
      "id": "mixed-signals",
      "description": "One event with pins, popular photos, a 3-photo capture burst, and cold photos. Golden top-8: two pins (newest first), popularity descending, then the burst (newest first), then the single low-engagement photo. holdout_picks = the admin's plausible selection; top-6 precision = 5/6 = 0.833.",
